      "versionNonce": 609850778,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779961706795,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "firstly, based on the comparison with l we can\ndetermine if m is in the left or right section\nif left (m > l):\n    if l<=target<=m:\n        binary search within l and m\n    else:\n        go left (l=m+1)\nelse (m < l; m is in right section)\n    if m<=target<=r\n        binary search withni m and r\n    else\n        go right (r=m-1)\n\nnow the quetsion is how do we integrate that\n'binary search within....' stuff into the loop so\nthat we dont have to write two separate\nprocedures\ni guess youd just put the comparison logic\ndirectly in there. so for 'binary search within l\nand m' right",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "firstly, based on the comparison with l we can determine if m is in the left or right section\nif left (m > l):\n    if l<=target<=m:\n        binary search within l and m\n    else:\n        go left (l=m+1)\nelse (m < l; m is in right section)\n    if m<=target<=r\n        binary search withni m and r\n    else\n        go right (r=m-1)\n\nnow the quetsion is how do we integrate that 'binary search within....' stuff into the loop so that we dont have to write two separate procedures\ni guess youd just put the comparison logic directly in there. so for 'binary search within l and m' right",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
